From right triangle $WYZ$, we have $\tan Z = \frac{WY}{ZY}$, so $WY = ZY\cdot \tan Z = 12\cdot 1.5 = 18$.  From right triangle $WXY$, we have $\tan X = \frac{WY}{WX}$, so \[WX = \frac{WY}{\tan X} = \frac{18}{3} = 6.\]Therefore, the area of $WXYZ$ is \[\frac{WX+YZ}{2}\cdot WY = 9\cdot 18 = \boxed{270}.\]

